Z||000000||Roy||05-11-99||04:16 PM||||Well last night my fiero with its brand new paint job got egg'd pretty good:( I got the egg off in time, I saw it when I was walking the dog. This is the third time. Is there any product you guys know of that can protect your paint on your car from eggs and the balonie and such? This is starting to be a pain in the a$$. The cops have been no help what so ever. I even set up a camcorder but it happends what seems to be maybe once every six months, so thats a lot of time and effort. I can't garage it do to I have a project car in the garage. Any idea's? I desperatly need to somehow put a end to this. Sorry if this topic is a little off topic.
Z||000001||PaUL||05-11-99||04:25 PM||||I got egged once. This was at night, I heard a loud bang and this crap splattered all over my windshield. At first I didnt know what it was, I thought it was some kind of glue bomb, well the egg looked like glue at night. Later I looked at the spot the egg hit, it was right on the drivers side windshield frame. It made an impression on the paint, and I am sure it would have cracked the windshield if it hit a few inches to the right. I guess I was lucky that they hit my car where they did. 
Z||000002||Patrick||05-11-99||04:27 PM||||<br>Well, my first suggestion would be a <b>shotgun</b>. But being from Canada, we're not supposed to think that way here.<p>I don't know what else to suggest other than to get it off the street. In the past I've had my share of problems too, so I know how damn frustrating it can be.<p>I know this is not what you're after, but you've got my sympathy.<p>
Z||000003||Pretender||05-11-99||06:20 PM||||Ever since my tape deck was stolen, and that was a mess, the punks had to bend my auto stick back by foot to have the clearence to pull out the unit!,anyways i went out to WAL-MART and bought a car cover, it doesn't really protect against theifs if they really want to get into the car but it does keep out the birdy poo and those annoying little "heli-copters" from that darn tree out front.
Z||000004||theogre||05-11-99||08:28 PM||||well applied wax or if your paint is in good shape some of the silcone or polymer protectors. anything to keep the egg directly off the paint.<p>Never allow egg to age on the paint..... it Will do permanat damage. If any cop ever tells you egg doesn't do permanat damage have hit let one site on his own car for a day or 3..... He'll be more than willing to arrest any little ~!@#$%^&*(_)(*&^%$#@! he catches doing it the next time.
Z||000005||Cliff Pennock||05-13-99||02:27 AM||||I've been considering all kinds of stuff also: motion sensitive alarms, camcorders from my apartment, camcorders <b>inside</b> the car, etc. Here in Holland it's even worse than throwing eggs. A car like this attracks all sorts of attacks. Usually it's a scratch made with a nail or key, but often enough they put glue in the locks, scratch the paint with a rock, break off the antenna, break off the mirrors, break a window or whatever. I guess it happens about once a week.<p>And the police doesn't want to do anything about it, they say they have more important things to do (which means they have parking tickets to write, donuts to eat and soccer games to watch). Yeah, the police is a real help here in Holland. Once the burglary alarm of my neighbour went off and I called the police. Their response was to go check it out myself. I told them I wasn't planning on walking in om some armed thiefs and that it was their job to go check it out. They never came and the next morning my neighbours shop was emptied out. A few months later, my other neighbours alarm went off. I called them again and this time they did come - to cut the wire of the alarm because it was making such a noise!!!
Z||000006||PaUL||05-13-99||01:41 PM||||Wow, what kind of police dept you got there in Holland? Thats the worst dereliction of duty I ever heard of. I bet the police in Russia are better. 
Z||000007||sluppy123||05-13-99||06:46 PM||||I feel your pain roy!!!<p>I had a similar problem with kids screwing with my car also, however i saw them doing it!! I called the cops but they said that there was no property damage done and they couldn't do anything about it. So i declared marshal law and took care of the problem myself. Now there's one rice-grinder running around less one mirror. REVENG IS SWEET!!!!!
